00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:03.236
Bl<00:00:00.666><c>ad</c><00:00:00.699><c>es</c><00:00:00.733><c>mi</c><00:00:00.766><c>th</c><00:00:00.799><c>s,</c>
<00:00:00.900><c>we</c><00:00:00.933><c>lc</c><00:00:00.966><c>om</c><00:00:01.000><c>e </c><00:00:01.033><c>to</c><00:00:01.066><c> t</c><00:00:01.100><c>he</c><00:00:01.133><c> k</c><00:00:01.166><c>il</c><00:00:01.200><c>l </c><00:00:01.233><c>te</c><00:00:01.267><c>st</c><00:00:01.300><c>.</c>

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:06.271
To define what kind of
lethal damage they will do,

00:00:06.305 --> 00:00:08.140
I'm going to take your weapons

00:00:08.207 --> 00:00:10.377
and deliver some lethal blows
to this ballistics dummy.

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:12.879
Jacob, you're up first, ready?

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:14.381
-Cut the head off.
-Let's do that.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.778
All right.

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:48.147
Jacob, let's talk about
your sickle sword right here.

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:51.417
Your edge is razor-sharp coupled
with the fact

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.486
that this is
a very light weapon.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:57.490
I can use velocity
to really wield that sharp edge.

00:00:57.523 --> 00:01:00.226
It cuts deep into
this ballistics dummy,

00:01:00.259 --> 00:01:04.297
and overall, sir,
your weapon will kill.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.165
-Thank you.
-All right.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:07.500
Robert, your turn, sir,
you ready?

00:01:07.533 --> 00:01:09.269
-I'm ready.
-Let's do this.

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:37.763
All right. Robert, let's talk
about your sickle sword.

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:39.498
It's a very light blade,

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.334
that much lighter
than the other one,

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:44.437
and the angle that you have
in here lends itself to use

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:46.605
not only velocity
but the sharpness of your edge

00:01:46.672 --> 00:01:49.876
to cut very deep
into this ballistics dummy,

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:53.546
and overall, sir,
you'll kill.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:55.215
Thank you.

00:01:58.684 --> 00:02:00.820
Bladesmiths, welcome
to the strength test,

00:02:00.853 --> 00:02:03.923
the armored warrior chop.
To test the strength

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:07.160
and overall durability of
your Mesopotamian sickle swords,

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:10.429
I'm going to be chopping
into these armored warriors.

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:12.465
Jacob, you're up first.
You ready for this?

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:14.767
-I don't think I get a choice.
-You don't have a choice.

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:43.396
Come on.

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:55.441
What actually happened is,

00:02:55.474 --> 00:02:57.376
your sword bit into
the other sword

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:00.547
by about 3/16ths of an inch,
and it took out this chip,

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:03.316
and once that chip was gone,
the whole sword blew up.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.319
Your grain looks good,

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:09.822
but unfortunately it's just
this sword against that sword.

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:11.824
That time, that sword won.

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:17.596
-Yep.
-All right. Jacob,

00:03:17.629 --> 00:03:19.899
we hate to see this happen.
You gave us a beautiful blade,

00:03:19.932 --> 00:03:22.901
but unfortunately it did
suffer catastrophic failure

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:24.470
on the seventh strike,

00:03:24.503 --> 00:03:26.438
but you are not out
of the fight yet

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:28.174
because, Robert, in order
to become the champion,

00:03:28.241 --> 00:03:31.010
you will have to survive
every single one of those

00:03:31.076 --> 00:03:32.778
seven strikes
on the armored warrior.

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:34.146
Are you ready?

00:03:34.213 --> 00:03:35.748
-Let's roll the dice.
-All right, Ben.

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:04.611
Good job.

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:12.818
Well, Robert, the big thing is,
it's one sword, nice job.

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:14.487
Thank you.

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:18.691
Well, Robert, you made it
through all the testing.

00:04:18.724 --> 00:04:20.726
Jacob, it's a beautiful
piece of work.

00:04:20.759 --> 00:04:22.561
Unfortunately due to
your catastrophic failure,

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:24.464
we cannot continue testing it.
For that reason,

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:27.399
I'm going to have to ask you to
please step off the forge floor.

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:29.035
Thank you, gentlemen.
It was an honor.

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:30.970
-Thank you very much.
-Very nice job.

00:04:31.037 --> 00:04:33.806
Thank you.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.908 size:78% position:39%
It totally sucks,

00:04:35.941 --> 00:04:39.012
but I really am proud
of the blade I made either way.

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:42.181
They said pretty much nothing
but good things about it up

00:04:42.214 --> 00:04:45.318
until it broke, and, well,
I'd totally come back for this

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:47.954
and maybe get a shot at
making it all the way through.

00:04:49.955 --> 00:04:52.759
Robert, we never like to see
competitors' blades break,

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:54.527
but yours did not,

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.429
and that makes you the newest
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:04:56.496 --> 00:05:00.132
You just got yourself a check
for $10,000, congratulations.

00:05:00.166 --> 00:05:02.935
-Thanks, thanks.
-Feel pretty good?

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:06.639
Crazy, dude, crazy.
Winning this championship

00:05:06.672 --> 00:05:09.309
I think has really pushed me
to my limits,

00:05:09.342 --> 00:05:11.010
and then that makes me
want to push them even more.

00:05:11.043 --> 00:05:12.644
Now I'm a champion.

00:05:12.678 --> 00:05:14.680
I'm going to go ahead
and get my ABS smith membership

00:05:14.714 --> 00:05:16.549
and just really refine
my skills.

